#: ../../source/index.rst:5
#: 37279f4be101489bb60a2d532199bbd1
msgid "MAVProxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:7
#: 506cdd848dbc422eb9f0061f3b7a059b
msgid "**A UAV ground station software package for MAVLink based systems**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:9
#: 6ab75858073c415ea251c685d435db01
msgid "MAVProxy is a fully-functioning GCS for UAV's, designed as a minimalist, portable and extendable GCS for any autonomous system supporting the MAVLink protocol (such as one using ArduPilot). MAVProxy is a powerful command-line based “developer” ground station software.  It can be extended via add-on modules, or complemented with another ground station, such as Mission Planner, APM Planner 2, QGroundControl etc, to provide a graphical user interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:14
#: b20a9537f4b84e82804908b26d44ad54
msgid "It has a number of key features, including the :ref:`ability to forward the messages<mavproxy-forwarding>` from your UAV over the network via UDP to multiple other ground station software on other devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:16
#: f8f45fb84ba04577b56d09212b1fd9dc
msgid "MAVProxy is commonly used by developers (especially with SITL) for testing new builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:18
#: e0785a5ecebc4cabbf0666ccdc9dbeff
msgid "MAVProxy was first developed by `CanberraUAV <http://www.canberrauav.org.au>`_, to enable the use of companion computing and multiple datalinks with ArduPilot. It has grown to be one of the most versatile tools in the ArduPilot ecosystem, and many of the features users now see in other GCS tools can trace their origins to MAVProxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:25
#: 378cccdc4e73466cb3ae54512c0f2190
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:27
#: 1347c8e9df6e46f384aa834a39cfc535
msgid "It is a command-line, console based app. There are plugins included in MAVProxy to provide a basic GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:29
#: 9afa066cf4b8472aa014896f03c35315
msgid "Can be networked and run over any number of computers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:30
#: a09794457edb442f8d0e97c4cac67010
msgid "It's portable; it should run on any POSIX OS with python, pyserial, and ``select()`` function calls, which means Linux, OS X, Windows, and others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:33
#: 24cabab8d2424b0b82ffd231703d50c9
msgid "The light-weight design means it can run on small netbooks with ease."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:34
#: 4c13b41436bc45329d8a81b35074772b
msgid "It supports loadable modules, and has modules to support console/s, moving maps, joysticks, antenna trackers, etc"
msgstr ""

